5. Modding

The Project Owner expressly permits and encourages Mods.

Anyone may create Mods for the Project using Project Materials, subject to the terms of this License.

Mods may include modifications to existing files, new files, replacement files, scripts, code, assets, plugins, patches, or other material intended to alter or extend the Project.

Mod creators retain ownership of their own original creative work contained in their Mods, subject to the ownership rights of the Project Owner in the underlying Project Materials.

6. Ownership of Modifications

The Project Owner retains ownership of the original Project Materials contained within a Mod.

A Mod creator owns the copyright in original material they independently create and add to the Project, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

For example, if a Mod creator modifies a Project-owned source file, the Project Owner continues to own the original Project code while the Mod creator owns their original modifications to that code.

Creating a Mod does not transfer ownership of the Project or its original materials to the Mod creator.

Likewise, modifying a Project-owned file does not cause the Mod creator to acquire ownership of the original Project material contained within that file.

